{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastScanner in = new FastScanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        new Solver().solve(in, out);\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    static class FastScanner {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        FastScanner(InputStream in) {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    String line = br.readLine();\n                    if (line == null) return null;\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(line);\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(e);\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class Solver {\n        final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n        final long INF = (long) 1e18 + 1;\n        long[][] C = new long[100][100];\n\n        long f(long p, int a, int b, int c, int d) {\n            p = p * C[a][b] % MOD;\n            p = p * C[c][d] % MOD;\n            return p;\n        }\n\n        void solve(FastScanner in, PrintWriter out) {\n            int n = in.nextInt();\n            int K = in.nextInt();\n            for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {\n                    if (j == 0 || j == i) C[i][j] = 1;\n                    else C[i][j] = (C[i - 1][j] + C[i - 1][j - 1]) % MOD;\n                }\n            }\n            int cnt1 = 0, cnt2 = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                if (in.nextInt() == 50) cnt1++;\n                else cnt2++;\n            }\n            long[][][] dist = new long[200][200][2];\n            long[][][] dp = new long[200][200][2];\n            for (int i = 0; i < 200; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < 200; j++) {\n                    Arrays.fill(dist[i][j], INF);\n                }\n            }\n            dist[0][0][0] = 0;\n            dp[0][0][0] = 1;\n            ArrayDeque<State> q = new ArrayDeque<>();\n            q.add(new State(0, 0, 0));\n            while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n                State cur = q.poll();\n                int x = cur.x;\n                int y = cur.y;\n                int z = cur.z;\n                long d = dist[x][y][z];\n                if (z == 0) {\n                    int rx = cnt1 - x;\n                    int ry = cnt2 - y;\n                    for (int a = 0; a <= rx; a++) {\n                        for (int b = 0; b <= ry; b++) {\n                            if (a + b == 0) continue;\n                            if (a * 50 + b * 100 > K) break;\n                            int nx = x + a;\n                            int ny = y + b;\n                            int nz = 1;\n                            if (dist[nx][ny][nz] >= d + 1) {\n                                long add = f(dp[x][y][z], rx, a, ry, b);\n                                if (dist[nx][ny][nz] > d + 1) {\n                                    dist[nx][ny][nz] = d + 1;\n                                    q.add(new State(nx, ny, nz));\n                                }\n                                dp[nx][ny][nz] = (dp[nx][ny][nz] + add) % MOD;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    int rx = x;\n                    int ry = y;\n                    for (int a = 0; a <= rx; a++) {\n                        for (int b = 0; b <= ry; b++) {\n                            if (a + b == 0) continue;\n                            if (a * 50 + b * 100 > K) break;\n                            int nx = x - a;\n                            int ny = y - b;\n                            int nz = 0;\n                            if (dist[nx][ny][nz] >= d + 1) {\n                                long add = f(dp[x][y][z], rx, a, ry, b);\n                                if (dist[nx][ny][nz] > d + 1) {\n                                    dist[nx][ny][nz] = d + 1;\n                                    q.add(new State(nx, ny, nz));\n                                }\n                                dp[nx][ny][nz] = (dp[nx][ny][nz] + add) % MOD;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (dist[cnt1][cnt2][1] == INF) out.println(-1);\n            else out.println(dist[cnt1][cnt2][1]);\n            out.println(dp[cnt1][cnt2][1]);\n        }\n\n        static class State {\n            int x, y, z;\n\n            State(int x, int y, int z) {\n                this.x = x;\n                this.y = y;\n                this.z = z;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 1.0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<trans